From 089e55c0773dd6c1c3a86ef0260473a0f4ed4259 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drew Moseley <drew@moseleynet.net>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 15:59:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] arm: k3: board: dts: Add Toradex Aquila AM69 SoM support

Port Toradex Aquila AM69 (AM69 / J784S4 SoC) board support to the
TI u-boot-ti 2025.01 tree.

- arch/arm/mach-k3/j784s4/Kconfig: add TARGET_AQUILA_AM69_A72/R5
- board/toradex/aquila-am69/: Kconfig, Makefile, board C code,
  DDR timing tables (8/16/32 GB), YAML system configs
  (board-cfg, pm-cfg, rm-cfg, sec-cfg, tifs-rm-cfg)
- include/configs/aquila-am69.h: SDRAM base addresses
- arch/arm/dts/: R5 DTS, u-boot DTSI (binman, SPL fixups),
  LPDDR4-4266 DDR timing DTSI
- dts/upstream/src/arm64/ti/: A72 SoM DTSI and dev-board DTS
  (OF_UPSTREAM path for TI 2025.01)
- configs/aquila-am69_{a72,r5}_defconfig: initial defconfigs

dram_init() calls k3_mem_map_init() directly: TI boards inherit
dram_init() from board/ti/common/k3-ddr.c (linked via
HAVE_VENDOR_COMMON_LIB = board/ti/common/), which does not apply to
VENDOR=toradex. Without populating k3_mem_map[] with cacheable DRAM
entries before enable_caches() builds the ARM64 page tables, the MMU
faults on any access above 0x80000000 and the board hangs silently
inside enable_caches().

Signed-off-by: Drew Moseley <drew.moseley@toradex.com>
